      vignette: "A synthetic 74-year-old with Parkinson disease treated with levodopa had emergency bowel surgery two days ago and has been nil by mouth since; none of his Parkinson medicines have been given. He is now confused, sweating, and has a temperature of 39.6 C, heart rate 124, and blood pressure swinging between 90/50 and 170/95. He is severely rigid all over. Creatine kinase is markedly raised. The wound looks clean.",
